<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop-rdf v0.3.0 tag does not build under SLOP 0.3.0" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The slop-rdf v0.3.0 tag fails SLOP 0.3.0's type check with \"cannot push to a field of parameter 'g'\" in graph-add and graph-add-unchecked, which now require `(mut g Graph)`. The fix (c14fe19) was released as slop-rdf v0.4.0, which is what slop-rdf-sys 0.4.0 vendors. Before each regeneration, check that the chosen slop-rdf tag type-checks under the target SLOP version; don't assume an older tag still compiles after a SLOP upgrade." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f2df56db-c064-49fa-bb08-700336cf6a24> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T06:47:45.051353Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "slop-rdf v0.3.0 tag does not build under SLOP 0.3.0" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop-rdf v0.3.0 tag does not build under SLOP 0.3.0" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The slop-rdf v0.3.0 tag fails SLOP 0.3.0's type check with \"cannot push to a field of parameter 'g'\" in graph-add and graph-add-unchecked, which now require `(mut g Graph)`. The fix is slop-rdf commit c14fe19 (untagged, v0.3.0+4). slop-rdf-sys 0.3.2 vendors that commit and records it as slop-rdf-commit metadata. Before each regeneration, check that the pinned slop-rdf ref type-checks under the target SLOP version; don't assume the latest tag is compatible." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T06:44:28.740728Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "slop-rdf v0.3.0 tag does not build under SLOP 0.3.0" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/7a1b9928-bedb-4c39-8a66-113b489bfddc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/63167b7b-21eb-406c-87b5-7b41b03a9df8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c0f6e634-c5aa-46e4-ae83-34c65b60f4b9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c0f6e634-c5aa-46e4-ae83-34c65b60f4b9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MSRV CI needs MSRV-aware dependency resolution" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c0f6e634-c5aa-46e4-ae83-34c65b60f4b9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c0f6e634-c5aa-46e4-ae83-34c65b60f4b9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The Rust 1.63 CI job must generate its lockfile with stable Cargo and CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_RUST_VERSIONS=fallback, then run `cargo +1.63.0 test`. Cargo 1.63 predates MSRV-aware resolution and pulls the newest build dependencies even when they need a newer rustc. cc 1.4.3+ and find-msvc-tools 0.1.10+ require rustc 1.65, and that broke the MSRV job on main from Aug 2026. With rust-version = 1.63, stable Cargo selects cc 1.4.0 / find-msvc-tools 0.1.9 and writes a v3 lockfile, which Cargo 1.63 can read. Pinning individual crates with `cargo update --precise` was rejected because each new transitive release breaks it again. Raising rust-version to 1.65 was left to the maintainer because it changes the published MSRV promise. Downstream users building on 1.63 with an old Cargo need to pin these crates themselves." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c0f6e634-c5aa-46e4-ae83-34c65b60f4b9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c0f6e634-c5aa-46e4-ae83-34c65b60f4b9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T06:58:30.486467Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/c0f6e634-c5aa-46e4-ae83-34c65b60f4b9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "MSRV CI needs MSRV-aware dependency resolution" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Regenerate csrc/src with `slop build --library static`, keep the generated C, and vendor it with each crate version matching its upstream (slop-std-sys = SLOP version, slop-rdf-sys = slop-rdf version; [package.metadata.slop-sys] records slop-version/slop-rdf-version).\n\nProcedure:\n1. The slop CLI writes C to tempfile.TemporaryDirectory, so run it through a small Python wrapper (using the slop-lang uv tool interpreter, `python -I`) that replaces TemporaryDirectory with a persistent directory and then calls slop.cli.main with [\"slop\",\"build\",...]. The installed CLI uses the native parser/compiler from ~/code/slop/bin, so that checkout must be at the target SLOP tag.\n2. slop-rdf-sys: `git archive` the slop-rdf tag into a scratch directory and build it there with its own slop.toml. That build is also the type check against the target SLOP; `slop check` only takes a single file. Copy the 10 module .c/.h pairs (rdf, index, list, vocab, xsd, common, ttl, n3, serialize_ttl, serialize_n3).\n3. slop-std-sys: make a scratch library project (slop.toml type=static, sources=[\"src\"]) with lib/std/strlib/strlib.slop, lib/std/io/file.slop and lib/std/thread/thread.slop taken from the SLOP tag via `git show`. Use a multi-module build; a single-module build of thread leaves no C behind. Copy slop_{strlib,file,thread}.{c,h}. The strlib/file C from the rdf build should be byte-identical, which makes a useful cross-check.\n4. Post-process: rewrite `#include \"slop_runtime.h\"` to `#include \"../runtime/slop_runtime.h\"` in the regenerated files only. Copy src/slop/runtime/slop_runtime.h from the SLOP tag into both crates' csrc/runtime. slop_std_shim.c is hand-written and must never be overwritten; check that the runtime's slop_arena_new/slop_arena_free/slop_intern_string signatures still match it.\n5. Verify with the RELEASING.md preflight, the MSRV job (CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_RUST_VERSIONS=fallback lockfile + cargo +1.63.0 test), and a full-archive link: force-load libslop_rdf.a and libslop_std.a from target/ into a trivial C main.\n\nApplied for SLOP 0.3.0 + slop-rdf 0.4.0 (slop-lang/slop-sys#1) and SLOP 0.4.0 + slop-rdf 0.5.0 (branch slop-0.4.0)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-10-06T02:30:40.067617Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The csrc/src trees are regenerated with `slop build` in static-library mode, and the generated C is kept. The slop CLI writes C to a tempfile.TemporaryDirectory, so the build is run through a small Python wrapper that swaps in a persistent directory. slop-rdf-sys is built from the slop-rdf repo's slop.toml at a tagged release. slop-std-sys comes from a scratch library project containing lib/std strlib.slop, io/file.slop and thread.slop from the SLOP tag; a single-module `slop build` of lib/std/thread takes a different code path and leaves no C behind. Post-processing: rewrite `#include \"slop_runtime.h\"` to `#include \"../runtime/slop_runtime.h\"` in every .c and .h. Copy src/slop/runtime/slop_runtime.h from the SLOP tag into both crates' csrc/runtime. slop_std_shim.c is hand-written and must never be overwritten. Crate versions match upstream: slop-std-sys = SLOP version, slop-rdf-sys = slop-rdf version. [package.metadata.slop-sys] records slop-version and slop-rdf-version. Applied for SLOP 0.3.0 + slop-rdf 0.4.0 (PR slop-lang/slop-sys#1)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T06:47:44.976199Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/36ce0090-c66a-4cc6-ad84-49871f9f9249> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The csrc/src trees are regenerated with `slop build` in static-library mode, and the generated C is kept. The slop CLI writes C to a tempfile.TemporaryDirectory, so the build is run through a small Python wrapper that swaps in a persistent directory. slop-rdf-sys is built from the slop-rdf repo's slop.toml. slop-std-sys comes from a scratch library project containing lib/std strlib.slop, io/file.slop and thread.slop from the SLOP tag; a single-module `slop build` of lib/std/thread takes a different code path and leaves no C behind. Post-processing: rewrite `#include \"slop_runtime.h\"` to `#include \"../runtime/slop_runtime.h\"` in every .c and .h. Copy src/slop/runtime/slop_runtime.h from the SLOP tag into both crates' csrc/runtime. slop_std_shim.c is hand-written and must never be overwritten. Crate versions: slop-std-sys tracks the SLOP version; slop-rdf-sys gets a patch bump when the public headers are unchanged. Record slop-version, slop-rdf-version and slop-rdf-commit in [package.metadata.slop-sys]. First applied for SLOP 0.3.0 (PR slop-lang/slop-sys#1)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T06:44:28.578104Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9056e533-0d1c-4fc5-97c5-40849b001f24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/82129cf6-b55d-4d8b-9eac-fe5bd795b7e9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "slop-rdf was tagged v0.4.0 at the vendored commit c14fe19. The repo convention (commit 7d218ee) is that each -sys crate version matches its upstream library version, so slop-rdf-sys became 0.4.0 instead of a patch bump, and the slop-rdf-commit pin was dropped in favor of the tag." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T06:47:44.976199Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/137fc998-b2bc-44d5-a9e9-57bdd379bc9f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Vendored C regeneration via slop library build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/74bacec7-9e27-4b30-a751-89e3431b5c48> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Applied again for SLOP 0.4.0 + slop-rdf 0.5.0. The procedure is refined with exact source paths, the type-check step (`slop check` needs a single file, so `slop build` is the project-level check), the native-toolchain dependency on the ~/code/slop checkout, and a full-archive link verification. The link tests alone only pull in a few objects." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
